---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { resolvePath } from '../utils/paths';
---

<BaseLayout title="Report a correction — Life as Usual" description="How to report a wrong, outdated or unsafe tip in the India edition, and what happens to your report.">
  <div class="page-shell correction-shell">
    <p class="eyebrow">Corrections</p>
    <h1>Tell us where we are wrong</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      This edition carries inherited claims, automated adaptations and a recorded owner self-review. It is not professionally
      verified. If a tip is outdated, misquoted, unsafe, or says something about India that the official source does not support,
      a correction report is the fastest way to get it fixed.
    </p>

    <section class="info-card liquid-glass">
      <h2 class="card-heading">What to include</h2>
      <ul class="clean-list">
        <li>The page address, or the tip number shown on the card (for example 7-13).</li>
        <li>The exact sentence that is wrong, quoted.</li>
        <li>What the correct position is, and a link to the official source that shows it.</li>
        <li>The date you checked the source, and whether it applies in every state or only some.</li>
      </ul>
      <p class="small">
        Leave out personal details. Never send Aadhaar, bank account, card, policy or medical record numbers. Reports live in a
        public issue tracker, so anything you post is public.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="info-card liquid-glass">
      <h2 class="card-heading">How to send it</h2>
      <p>
        Open a correction report on GitHub. It creates a public issue with the fields above.
      </p>
      <p>
        <a class="btn btn-primary" href="https://github.com/RohannShetty/LifeAsUsual/issues/new?template=correction.yml" rel="noopener noreferrer">
          Open a correction report
        </a>
      </p>
      <p class="small">
        If you cannot use GitHub, a message to the repository owner through GitHub is the only other supported route. There is
        no email address, contact form or support desk for this edition, and this page does not pretend otherwise.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="info-card liquid-glass">
      <h2 class="card-heading">What happens next</h2>
      <ol class="clean-list ordered">
        <li>The report is checked against the current official source, not against another summary.</li>
        <li>If the source supports the correction, the tip text is fixed, the source link is replaced, and the correction is logged in the public corrections log with the checking date.</li>
        <li>If the claim cannot be checked, the tip is marked as unverified or held rather than silently kept as fact.</li>
        <li>If the report is wrong or the source does not support it, the report is closed with the reason and the source that was read.</li>
      </ol>
      <p class="small">
        This is a small, single-editor project. Reports are handled in best-effort order with safety and money claims first.
        No response time is promised, and no report is treated as professional review or approval.
      </p>
      <p>
        <a class="link" href="https://github.com/RohannShetty/LifeAsUsual/blob/master/docs/corrections-log.md" rel="noopener noreferrer">Read the corrections log</a>
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="info-card liquid-glass">
      <h2 class="card-heading">If the problem is urgent</h2>
      <p>
        This site cannot help in an emergency. For immediate danger call 112. For a financial fraud in progress, use the
        national cybercrime portal at cybercrime.gov.in or call 1930. Do not wait for a correction report.
      </p>
    </section>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .correction-shell { max-width: 48rem; margin: 0 auto; padding: 3rem 1.25rem 6rem; display: grid; gap: 1.25rem; }
  .correction-shell h1 { font-size: clamp(1.9rem, 5vw, 2.8rem); line-height: 1.1; }
  .eyebrow { text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.12em; font-size: 0.75rem; color: var(--color-jade); font-family: var(--font-sans); }
  .lede { font-size: 1.05rem; color: var(--color-ink-muted); max-width: 40rem; }
  .small { font-size: 0.875rem; color: var(--color-ink-muted); margin-top: 0.75rem; }
  .clean-list.ordered { list-style: decimal; }
</style>